            <ArticleTitle>Pain syndromes in patients with cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>169-84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of common pain syndromes in patients with pain and cancer includes pain associated with direct tumor infiltration, pain resulting from cancer therapy, and pain unrelated to the cancer or cancer therapy. Appropriate management is dependent on their careful evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
